From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Olexandr Tyshchenko <o.tyshchenko@eslua.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: vsi: take the old domain in attach_dev

Linux 6.18.57 backports fd714986e4e4 ("iommu: Pass in old domain to
attach_dev callback functions"), so the attach_dev callback takes the
old domain as a third argument. Update the two callbacks of the
VeriSilicon IOMMU driver that Armbian's media-0007 patch adds.

This is the fix of armbian/build db9f6c5120 ("rockchip64-6.18: fix broken
iommu driver patch"), as a separate patch on top of the Armbian v26.5.1
one: in v26.5.1 a user patch with the same name does not replace the
core one.
---
--- a/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
@@ -491,7 +491,7 @@
 }
 
 static int vsi_iommu_identity_attach(struct iommu_domain *domain,
-				     struct device *dev)
+				     struct device *dev, struct iommu_domain *old)
 {
 	struct vsi_iommu *iommu = dev_iommu_priv_get(dev);
 	unsigned long flags;
@@ -566,7 +566,7 @@
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(vsi_iommu_restore_ctx);
 
 static int vsi_iommu_attach_device(struct iommu_domain *domain,
-				   struct device *dev)
+				   struct device *dev, struct iommu_domain *old)
 {
 	struct vsi_iommu *iommu = dev_iommu_priv_get(dev);
 	struct vsi_iommu_domain *vsi_domain = to_vsi_domain(domain);
